    "verdict": "REVISE",
    "summary": "Three material implementation defects remain in rate-limit and schema-error handling.",
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "REV-023",
        "severity": "medium",
        "path": "watcher.py:243-264, 300-317",
        "evidence": "The plan requires Telegram HTTP 429 to use its Retry-After value, but send_telegram_alert discards response headers and raises a generic HTTPError; flush_pending_alerts always schedules its generic exponential delay. A Telegram 429 with Retry-After=600 can therefore be retried after 40 seconds under default settings, contrary to the server directive and plan.",
        "fix": "Preserve the 429 status and Retry-After value (for example via a dedicated exception), then set next_attempt_at from that value; add a deterministic 429 test."
      },
      {
        "id": "REV-024",
        "severity": "medium",
        "path": "watcher.py:353-367, 379-387",
        "evidence": "compute_effective_interval limits average cycle frequency but main sends all route requests as an immediate sequential burst. With 100 configured routes and MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=60, it issues 100 requests at cycle start, already exceeding the configured per-minute budget before sleeping 100 seconds. This contradicts PLAN.md's claim that the budget cannot be exceeded by construction.",
        "fix": "Pace individual Travelpayouts requests with a shared monotonic rate limiter, or reject configurations whose route-count burst exceeds the configured budget."
      },
      {
        "id": "REV-025",
        "severity": "medium",
        "path": "watcher.py:136-157, 328-350",
        "evidence": "A successful HTTP response with valid JSON but an unexpected top-level shape (for example []), or data as a non-list, raises AttributeError at payload.get or item.get. That escapes check_route before flush_pending_alerts, so a pending alert for that route is not retried during the schema failure. The plan expressly requires unrecognized schemas to return None with an error signal while still flushing pending alerts.",
        "fix": "Validate that payload is a mapping and data is a list of mappings; log the schema error and return None so check_route reaches its unconditional flush. Add fixtures for top-level-list and malformed-data shapes."
      }
    ],
